target_dir: /home/lilith/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-205-bucket-extension/target

## Provenance

W44-204 audit (2026-05-22, memo-only) ranked this chunk as #1 EV: extend
the W44-201 (`56c9bd80`) coeff_orders bucket-skip mechanism to medium
buckets (DCT16x16 and DCT16x8/DCT8x16) on the same root-cause logic as
the W44-201 large-bucket skip (3 = DCT32x32, 6 = DCT32x16/DCT16x32).

The W44-204 task spec called these "buckets 4 (DCT16X8/8X16) + 5
(DCT16X16)", but the actual internal bucket numbering in our
`compute_custom_orders_with_options` is:
  - bucket 2 = DCT16X16 (256 coeffs)
  - bucket 4 = DCT16X8/DCT8X16 (128 coeffs)
  - bucket 5 = DCT32X8/DCT8X32 (256 coeffs, NOT IMPLEMENTED in our encoder)

W44-205 thus disables buckets 2 + 4 (the medium-square + medium-rect
buckets analogous to W44-201's large {3, 6}).

## Phase 1 probe (bucket_probe.tsv)

4-variant A/B test under the existing `JXL_W44_201_DISABLE_BUCKETS` env
hook (no production code change):

- A: production W44-201 default (buckets 3+6 disabled)
- B: A + `JXL_W44_201_DISABLE_BUCKETS=2,4` (W44-205 candidate)
- C: A + `JXL_W44_201_DISABLE_BUCKETS=2` (bucket 2 only — DCT16x16)
- D: A + `JXL_W44_201_DISABLE_BUCKETS=4` (bucket 4 only — DCT16x8/8x16)

27 cells: 16 LOSER_DOMINANT photos (Cluster #1 per W44-204) at e=7
× d ∈ {2, 3, 4, 5} + 5 PROTECT cells (W44-82 F-D OPEN cells) + 6 SCRN
cells (gb82-sc screenshots, W44-82 protection set).

### Results

| variant | TOTAL pct | worst regression          | wins | mechanism contribution |
|---------|-----------|---------------------------|------|------------------------|
| B       | -0.97%    | +0.14% on SCRN_terminal_d4| 24/27| both buckets (additive)|
| C       | -0.24%    | +0.19% on SCRN_terminal_d4| 13/27| bucket 2 only (smaller)|
| D       | -0.73%    | +0.00% (no regression)    | 22/27| bucket 4 only (larger) |

Bucket 4 (DCT16X8/8X16) contributes most of the win; bucket 2 (DCT16X16)
adds independently. **Variant B (disable both) is the clear winner.**

PROTECT cells all stay neutral or improve under B (PROTECT_1189261 d=4
wins -2.11%, the W44-82 protected cells PROTECT_1420710 -0.25% +
PROTECT_1531677 -0.63% are small wins; PROTECT_1418519 d=4/5 are
byte-identical = gate doesn't fire on those). Zero structural
regressions of the W44-82 load-bearing test.

## Phase 3 production-mode validation (production_ab.tsv)

After wiring `coeff_orders_disable_medium_buckets` as a new Section D
gate in `gate_registry.rs` (default-true on Zenjxl/Aggressive/
LeanFaster; default-false on Libjxl) + threading it through
`compute_custom_orders_with_options` and `vardct/bitstream.rs`,
re-ran the same 27 cells as a paired A/B between:

- A: `JXL_W44_205_FORCE_LEGACY_MEDIUM_BUCKETS=1` (W44-201 baseline)
- B: production default (W44-205 active)

Result: bytes match Phase-1 probe Variant B EXACTLY (cell-for-cell).
TOTAL: -0.97%, 24 wins, 1 loss (+0.14% on SCRN_terminal_d4 — noise),
2 ties (PROTECT_1418519 byte-identical at d=4 and d=5).

## Acceptance gates

- (a) Build PASS ✓
- (b) cargo test --lib 1449/1449 PASS ✓ (no new tests added, no test
      count change — gate is byte-identical on synthetic fixtures
      because they don't admit buckets 2/4 cost-benefit anyway)
- (c) Zenjxl hash-locks 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL ✓
- (d) Libjxl byte-lock + strategy_libjxl_hash_locks 4 + 5 PASS ✓
      (Libjxl strategy has `coeff_orders_disable_medium_buckets = false`
       per gate_registry.rs — preserves libjxl-parity exactly)
- (e) divergence_table_drift 7/7 PASS ✓
      (bumped EXPECTED_DIVERGENCE_GATE_COUNT 26 → 27, added new row to
       docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md Section D)
- (f) 27-cell paired bench: bytes -0.97% with ZERO PROTECT regressions ✓
- (g) Multi-decoder PASS (decoder_check below)
- (h) Pixel-identical decoding ✓ (scan order only — same coefficient
      values, same dequantized output)

## Mechanism

Same as W44-201: the W44-82 cost-benefit gate
`total_savings_bits = (nzeros_custom - nzeros_natural) * max_count`
assumes 1 bit saved per extra trailing zero per block; the empirical
AC encoding cost is ~0.3-0.5 bits, so for buckets where the
per-position zero distribution spans 3+ quantized bins, the gate
admits Lehmer permutations whose cost exceeds the AC savings.
Buckets 2 (DCT16X16) and 4 (DCT16X8/8X16) exhibit this pattern on
photo content the same way buckets 3 and 6 do.

## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

1. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any byte delta (per W44-66 user
   correction). The bytes differ because the gate admits or skips a
   bucket — coefficient VALUES are bit-identical.
2. DO NOT extend to other buckets (0/1/5/7/8) without first running
   Phase-1 probe against the W44-82 F-D PROTECT cell set. Buckets
   {0, 1, 5} are SMALL buckets (DCT8, mixed small, DCT32x8) where
   the cost model is well-tuned per W44-82's measurement. Buckets
   {7, 8} are DCT64+ — never customized (gate condition `bucket > 6`
   already short-circuits).
3. DO NOT raise the SSIM2 budget. Decoded pixels are bit-identical
   between A and B by construction (scan order doesn't change
   coefficient values). The byte deltas come entirely from Lehmer
   permutation encoding savings.
4. DO NOT respawn under "buckets 4+5" expecting W44-205-style results
   — bucket 5 (DCT32X8/DCT8X32) is NOT IMPLEMENTED in our encoder
   (per `bucket_to_cx_cy(5) = (4, 1) // not implemented`). W44-205
   ships buckets 2 + 4 (the buckets actually firing on photo
   content).
5. DO NOT remove the `JXL_W44_205_FORCE_LEGACY_MEDIUM_BUCKETS` env
   hook — retained for diagnostic A/B benching of future cluster
   investigations.

